part.text:
We added a call to createExplosion but haven't defined it, nor integrated particles into drawing and updating. Need to implement particle system: createExplosion that adds particles with position, velocity, size, lifetime, color. Update loop should move particles, shrink, remove when life <=0. Draw them.

Also we should improve ship graphics maybe use gradient, add slight glow. But minimal.

Add function createExplosion(m) after splitMeteor maybe before. Also adjust draw to render particles.

Let's edit: add createExplosion function after splitMeteor or above update.

Implementation: function createExplosion(m){ for(let i=0;i<10;i++){ const angle=Math.random()*2*Math.PI; const speed=Math.random()*2+1; particles.push({ x: m.x+m.size/2, y: m.y+m.size/2, vx: Math.cos(angle)*speed, vy: Math.sin(angle)*speed, radius: Math.random()*2+1, alpha:1, decay:0.02}); } }

Update: In update, after moving meteors, also update particles: particles.forEach(p=>{ p.x+=p.vx; p.y+=p.vy; p.alpha-=p.decay; p.radius*=0.98;}); particles = particles.filter(p=>p.alpha>0 && p.radius>0.2);

Need to declare particles variable already added.

Draw: after lasers maybe draw particles before UI: ctx.fillStyle='orange'; particles.forEach(p=>{ ctx.globalAlpha = p.alpha; ctx.beginPath(); ctx.arc(p.x,p.y,p.radius,0,Math.PI*2); ctx.fill();}); ctx.globalAlpha=1;

Also improve ship with gradient: use ctx.fillStyle = ctx.createLinearGradient(...). Let's just simple: after drawing ship set fillStyle = 'white'.

Ok implement edits.

